# UI rules

The bar is "best UX for a Kannada reader on a budget phone". Modern, calm, flat. No dated dashboard look.

## Tokens only

```tsx
// BAD — arbitrary values
<div className="bg-[#c8102e] text-[#fff] rounded-[7px]">

// GOOD — semantic tokens from src/styles/tokens.css
<div className="bg-accent text-on-accent rounded-md">
```

Semantic token families: `bg-*` (surface, elevated, paper), `text-*` (primary, secondary, muted, on-accent), `accent`, `border`, `radius-*`. Dark mode is automatic via `[data-theme="dark"]`; never branch on theme in components.

## Typography

- Reading text (books, definitions): `font-serif` → Noto Serif Kannada. UI chrome: `font-sans` → Anek Kannada.
- Never set Kannada text below 16px on mobile. Line-height ≥ 1.7 for Kannada body text (conjuncts need vertical room).
- Use the `<KannadaText>` component for any user-facing Kannada content so font-size scaling works everywhere.

## Layout & motion

- Mobile-first. Bottom navigation on small screens, top navigation on `md+`.
- Touch targets ≥ 44px. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`: every animation must have a reduced fallback.
- Animations are purposeful (page turn, sheet open). No decorative motion, gradients, or box-shadow stacks. One subtle elevation shadow token max.
- Loading: skeletons, not spinners, for content areas.

## Components

- Build from `src/components/ui/` primitives first. If a primitive is missing, add it there (one file, one component, props typed).
- Icons: inline SVG components in `src/components/icons/` (no icon packages). 24px grid, `currentColor`.
- Every interactive element has an accessible name (`aria-label` in Kannada via i18n when there is no visible text).
